#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/metafmt-rppx1:99:
#: ../include/uapi/linux/media/dreamchip/rppx1-config.h:540
msgid ""
"The Gamma Out Correction module is available on the Human Vision Output Pipe "
"(HV) and the Machine Vision Output Pipe (MV). Userspace selects which pipe "
"to operate by setting the **header.type** field to "
"RPPX1_PARAMS_BLOCK_TYPE_GA_HV or RPPX1_PARAMS_BLOCK_TYPE_GA_MV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/metafmt-rppx1:99:
#: ../include/uapi/linux/media/dreamchip/rppx1-config.h:545
msgid ""
"The module allows to apply a **gamma_y** gamma correction curve to RGB data "
"represented as a table of 16 entries. The 16 input sampling points can be "
"equidistant or segmented using a logarithmic scale according to the value of "
"**mode**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/metafmt-rppx1:99:
#: ../include/uapi/linux/media/dreamchip/rppx1-config.h:550
msgid ""
"The gamma curve values are 12 bits on the HV output pipe and 24 bits on the "
"MV output pipe. Userspace is expected to provide the curve values with a bit-"
"depth matching the one of pipe in use."
msgstr ""

